<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Assignment vs Equality: Confusion between = (assignment) and == (comparison).</li>
        <li>Global vs Local Scope: Believing a variable declared inside a function is accessible everywhere.</li>
        <li>Data Types: Assuming Python doesn't have data types because it's dynamically typed (students must understand that 5 and "5" are processed differently).</li>
        <li>Errors: Believing a program that runs has no errors (ignoring logic errors).</li>
    </ul>
</div>

